{"case_id":"T8049","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["state","configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["ares_addr_equal"],"reason":"H0 only passes one buffer to standalone ares_parse_*_reply APIs, while the changed static function ares_addr_equal belongs to cookie-server state handling and compares configured server addresses. It therefore cannot vary or compare two IPv6 server identities, exercise equal-versus-different address transitions, or cover the byte-level AF_INET6 representation implicated by the new nested-field comparison.","evidence":["The production change is in src/lib/ares_cookie.c and modifies the AF_INET6 branch of ares_addr_equal.","ares_addr_equal accepts two struct ares_addr values and first branches on addr1->family versus addr2->family.","The changed comparison reads addr6._S6_un._S6_u8 rather than the enclosing addr6 object, explicitly implicating IPv6 address bytes and structure padding.","H0 invokes only ares_parse_a_reply, ares_parse_aaaa_reply, ares_parse_ptr_reply, ares_parse_ns_reply, ares_parse_srv_reply, ares_parse_mx_reply, ares_parse_txt_reply, ares_parse_soa_reply, ares_parse_naptr_reply, ares_parse_caa_reply, and ares_parse_uri_reply; it creates no cookie state and supplies no pair of struct ares_addr values."],"recommended_action":"Add a stateful cookie-path harness that configures or selects IPv6 servers and generates pairs of addresses covering identical bytes, single-byte differences, different families, repeated server use, and server changes, so ares_addr_equal and the resulting cookie-server state transitions are exercised."}
